  ('3027487a-7a04-417e-b964-8fcdd2e823f8', 'a3b4c5d6-7e8f-4a21-8b01-1c2d3e4f5a31', null, 'topic'::public.curated_course_node_type, 'Scientific Realism and Anti-Realism', 'This central unit asks whether successful science gives us good reason to believe in unobservable entities and structures. Students compare realism, empiricism, instrumentalism, and structural realism. Students should be able to explain the strongest arguments on both sides of the realism debate.', 8),
